395 - As Birds Unto the Genial Homeland
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 395
Topic: Doctrines - 

Verse 1:
[G]As birds unto [D7]the [G]genial [D/F#]homeland [G]fly,
[F#dim]The [Em]winter's cold and [Bm/F#]low'ring [D/F#]skies to [Am]flee,
[D7/C]So [Bm]seeks [D7/A]my [G]soul [E7/D]Thy [Bm]gracious [Am]presence [G/D]here
[D7]And [Em]finds, [D7]O God, [G]its rest [Am]and [D]peace [G/D]in [D7]Thee.

Verse 2:
[G]Here at Thy [D7]shrine [G]we [D7/A]leave [G]all [D]vexing [G]care,
[F#dim]For [Em]get the disappointment, [D/F#]grief and [Am]tear,
[D7/C]And [Bm]on [D7/A]the [G]wings [E7/D]of [Am/C]hopeful song and [G/D]prayer
[D7]We [Em]rise, [D7]and rising [G/B]feel [Am]Thy [D]Spirit [D7]here.

Verse 3:
[G]Bless all who [D7]spend [G]this [D7/A]night [G]in [D]pain and [G]woe,
[F#dim]The [Em]burdened heart, the [Bm/F#]fainting, [D/F#]and distressed,
[D7/C]Thy [Bm]comfort [G]send [E7/D]to [Am/C]darkened homes bereaved,
[D7]Thy [Em]saving [D7]help [G]to those [Am]by [D]want [G/D]oppressed.

Verse 4:
[G]Come, Sabbath [D7]joy, [G]each [D7/A]trusting [D]heart now [G]fill,
[F#dim]And [Em]blissful peace within our [D/F#]homes abide,
[D7/C]May [Bm]thankful [G]praise [E7/D]each [Am/C]grateful heart now [G/D]thrill,
[D7]And [Em]to God's [D7]loving [G]care [Em]their [Am]lives [G/D]confide.
